║         MongoDB Docker Quick Reference                         ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

QUICK START (Docker Compose - Recommended):
  ./start-mongodb.sh              Start MongoDB
  ./start-mongodb.sh --with-admin Start with web UI (port 8081)
  ./stop-mongodb.sh               Stop (keep data)
  ./stop-mongodb.sh --remove-data Stop and delete all data

ALTERNATIVE (Simple Docker):
  ./docker-mongodb.sh start       Start MongoDB
  ./docker-mongodb.sh logs        View logs
  ./docker-mongodb.sh shell       Open MongoDB shell
  ./docker-mongodb.sh stop        Stop MongoDB
  ./docker-mongodb.sh remove      Remove everything

CONNECTION STRINGS:
  No Auth:   mongodb://localhost:27017/testdb
  With Auth: mongodb://admin:password@localhost:27017/testdb?authSource=admin

JAVA CLIENT:
  JVSReactiveMongoClient client = JVSReactiveMongoClient.builder()
      .connectionString("mongodb://localhost:27017")
      .database("testdb")
      .build();

WEB ADMIN (when started with --with-admin):
  URL:      http://localhost:8081
  Username: admin
  Password: admin

TROUBLESHOOTING:
  Port in use:           lsof -i :27017
  Check if running:      docker ps | grep mongodb
  View logs:             docker logs hitorro-mongodb
  Reset everything:      docker-compose down -v

